ery reference.\n- **Ready on merit (7):** TC-413 and TC-415 to TC-420. None can be flipped in this sitting: the registry copies are held, and every one of them verifies LLR-367, which has to be approved first. There's a text-only follow-up draft for this section too.\n\nI ran no test suites; this sitting rules on text, and both round-2 reviewers had run the lane's suites. I did confirm against the code that every cited test exists, which modules are slow, how the producer and the render behave, and that the derivation reads changed paths from the index on every route.\n\nI put each section's follow-up drafts under a `### Dispositions` subheading inside the verdict file, not in the spec, because the brief allowed only one committed file. The coordinator needs to carry them into the spec's `## Dispositions`, or answer them in the lane as WI-834's sitting 007 did.\n\nI left the owner's open question, whether `[product] test` must accept the appended arguments, unruled: neither section asked it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_read_input_tokens":226051,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240},"output_tokens":763,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62488e29-4f8f-46dc-a1ab-0647d367ffcd","uuid":"81f1b155-aa68-413f-ad1d-d06a7b7c20c4","timestamp":"2026-11-07T01:58:37.051Z","request_id":"req_011Cgnjqw86zEjJsTBUUvDtG"}
